// Rental income, for the year that just ended. The shipped `us` counts wages,
// interest, dividends and gains, and the gain on a sale; it has no Schedule E.
// What is here counts into the lines `us` reads (total-income), and the sale's
// depreciation recapture is the kind law of `rental-property` in accounts.ax.
//
// Simplifications, on purpose: cash method; the 25,000 USD passive-loss allowance
// is applied without its phase-out above 100,000 USD of income (this year's
// loss is used in full, because the sale of the whole interest frees it);
// recapture is taxed as ordinary income, which is right while the bracket is
// below 25%; no qualified business income deduction; no state tax.

/// Schedule E: rents received less everything under expenses/rental. A loss
/// offsets other income up to 25,000 USD (IRC §469(i)), and a loss on paper,
/// because of depreciation and interest, is common in the first year.
///
/// To fix: `axiom why rental-net` lists the rents and the expenses behind it.
law schedule-e
  each year closing 04-15
  let net = tally(rental-income) - tally(rental-expenses)
  count net as rental-net
  count max(net, empty - passive-allowance[year]) as total-income

/// Rents, late fees and kept deposits count when they arrive (cash method).
///
/// To fix: an amount that is not rent must arrive from another kind of place.
law count-rental-income
  on in
  when from is rent-income
  count amount as rental-income

// The passive-loss allowance for active participation in a rental (IRC §469(i)).
param passive-allowance
  2024 25_000 USD
  2025 25_000 USD
  2026 25_000 USD
